1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,222
Meet ClearRoute, a Canton Coin funding application for teams building on Canton.

2
00:00:05,222 --> 00:00:10,443
This walkthrough shows the current Devnet product and the intended transfer journey.

3
00:00:10,443 --> 00:00:13,489
We have verified the sender wallet connection.

4
00:00:13,489 --> 00:00:17,841
A complete transfer to a volunteer recipient is still pending.

5
00:00:18,875 --> 00:00:26,404
Small teams need a way to request C C, get a funding decision, and track what happened.

6
00:00:26,404 --> 00:00:29,505
ClearRoute brings that work into one application.

7
00:00:29,505 --> 00:00:33,491
The first pilot focuses on controlled wallet top ups.

8
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:36,591
Purchasing validator traffic is a separate operation.

9
00:00:37,625 --> 00:00:40,561
This is the actual public funding page.

10
00:00:40,561 --> 00:00:46,013
A builder can request Devnet Canton Coin without first creating a ClearRoute account.

11
00:00:46,013 --> 00:00:53,143
The form asks for a team name, contact email, full Canton Party I D, wallet provider, amount,

12
00:00:53,143 --> 00:00:54,401
and testing purpose.

13
00:00:54,401 --> 00:00:57,756
The page never asks for a private key.

14
00:00:58,792 --> 00:01:05,278
The recipient must use an onboarded Devnet wallet that can receive and accept Splice transfer offers.

15
00:01:05,278 --> 00:01:10,548
A party created in a participant console alone does not establish that capability.

16
00:01:10,548 --> 00:01:16,224
For a NODERS hosted wallet, the provider field can say NODERS slash Splice wallet.

17
00:01:16,224 --> 00:01:19,467
The first planned test is one C C.

18
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:26,119
The operator opens Demo transfers, checks the treasury wallet, and reviews the request.

19
00:01:26,119 --> 00:01:30,441
The operator verifies the recipient and records an approval decision.

20
00:01:30,441 --> 00:01:37,789
The pilot allows up to ten C C per request and one hundred C C of total

21
00:01:37,789 --> 00:01:40,382
reserved or delivered exposure, excluding fees.

22
00:01:40,382 --> 00:01:42,976
Approval itself does not transfer coins.

23
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:49,399
After approval and enabling sends, the operator submits a tracked transfer offer.

24
00:01:49,399 --> 00:01:55,248
The recipient opens their own wallet, verifies the sender and amount, and accepts.

25
00:01:55,248 --> 00:01:57,947
ClearRoute checks the original transfer status.

26
00:01:57,947 --> 00:02:04,696
If the outcome is uncertain, it reconciles that same transfer rather than submitting another payment.

27
00:02:04,696 --> 00:02:10,095
This sequence still needs a volunteer wallet for a complete live demonstration.

28
00:02:11,125 --> 00:02:18,219
Success means the application shows C C delivered with the wallet reported transaction reference, and the recipient

29
00:02:18,219 --> 00:02:19,054
confirms receipt.

30
00:02:19,054 --> 00:02:25,731
A click on Send, an approval, or a balance change alone is not our completion criterion.

31
00:02:25,731 --> 00:02:30,321
This video does not claim a completed native C C transfer.

32
00:02:31,333 --> 00:02:38,595
The latest verification run passed ninety one backend tests and forty three frontend tests, followed by the

33
00:02:38,595 --> 00:02:39,450
production build.

34
00:02:39,450 --> 00:02:44,149
The sender wallet identity, Devnet connection, and balance check also passed.

35
00:02:44,149 --> 00:02:50,129
Public pilot requests remain separate from the signed in customer funding page and billing.

36
00:02:50,129 --> 00:02:54,828
They are free Devnet tests and do not automatically create invoices.

37
00:02:55,833 --> 00:03:02,628
We are looking for one volunteer with a compatible NODERS Devnet wallet to receive a one C

38
00:03:02,628 --> 00:03:03,827
C test offer.

39
00:03:03,827 --> 00:03:08,223
Share only your full wallet Party I D and wallet provider.

40
00:03:08,223 --> 00:03:10,221
Never share passwords or tokens.

41
00:03:10,221 --> 00:03:13,418
ClearRoute helps builders request funding and track delivery.

42
00:03:13,418 --> 00:03:19,813
Visit the project repository linked in the description, and contact the builder to join the pilot.
